NAME
       sync, fsync, fdatasync - flush buffers to disk

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       void sync(void);
       int  cervus_sync(void);
       int  fsync(int fd);
       int  fdatasync(int fd);

DESCRIPTION
       Writes buffered data out to the device. sync flushes every
       filesystem; fsync flushes one file's data and metadata, and
       fdatasync skips metadata that does not affect reading the data
       back.

       Writes are buffered until then, so anything that must survive a
       power cut needs one of these. Unmounting and the shutdown path
       already flush.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

SEE ALSO
       truncate(2), write(2), mount(2), sync(1)
